	"@context": "tb",
	"data": "Walks\n\nStage 4 — Seye, after the cathedral\n\nThe floor stopped being a floor and started being a corridor.\n\nThis was not an improvement. Corridors have expectations. They expect you to walk somewhere. The cathedral of nothing had been spacious in its way — you could sit in apathy and not be going anywhere, and that was the whole point. A corridor has a direction. It wants you to follow it.\n\nSeye didn't want to follow it.\n\nThe fog pulsed, once, like a heartbeat. The walls of the corridor…",
